  "raw_text": "Step 1: Identify the values of m, n, p, and q from the given fractions.\nFor $\\frac{7}{30}@\\frac{10}{21}$, we have $m=7$, $n=30$, $p=10$, and $q=21$.\n\nStep 2: Substitute these values into the operation definition $\\frac{m}{n}@ \\frac{p}{q} = (m)(p)\\left(\\frac{q}{n}\\right)$.\nThis gives us $(7)(10)\\left(\\frac{21}{30}\\right)$.\n\nStep 3: Simplify the fraction $\\frac{21}{30}$.\n$\\frac{21}{30} = \\frac{7}{10}$.\n\nStep 4: Multiply the numbers together.\n$(7)(10)\\left(\\frac{7}{10}\\right) = 7 \\times 10 \\times \\frac{7}{10} = 7 \\times 7 = 49$.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{49}<|im_end|>",
